---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Ghost from "../../components/Ghost.astro";
import { DOC_ORDER, REPO } from "../../lib/site";
---

<Docs title="Docs" description="How to install Wisp, deploy it, give agents computers, and add any agent harness.">
  <h1>Wisp docs</h1>
  <p>
    Wisp has two parts. The <strong>hub</strong> holds your workspace: chats, agents, memory and files. One computer
    runs it. <strong>Devices</strong> are the computers that run your agents and their own computers (VMs). One computer
    can be both, and the desktop app sets that up for you.
  </p>
  <p>Just want to try it? <a href="/download/">Download the app</a> and follow the steps it shows.</p>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    {
      DOC_ORDER.map((d, i) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`/docs/${d.slug}/`}>
            <Ghost size={30} color="#ffffff" color2={["#5cc8ff", "#a98bff", "#4fd18b", "#ff9f6e"][i]} />
            <span>
              <strong>{d.title}</strong>
              <span class="blurb">{d.blurb}</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p>
    More is in the <a href={`${REPO}#readme`} rel="noopener">README on GitHub</a>: memory permissions, teams, and how
    agents decide what to load when they start.
  </p>
</Docs>

<style>
  .doc-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0 !important;
    margin: 24px 0 !important;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .doc-list a {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .doc-list a:hover {
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .doc-list strong {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .blurb {
    display: block;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
